  "output": {
    "answer": "The record shows they're checked against my own hands, not a live usability session. The method ends with a real-device check — I re-walk the built thing on one real device myself, and if it disagrees with the panel, the device wins. One open question I flagged is whether panel seconds-per-task is ever checked against a live stopwatch on my own sessions or only compared to itself before and after — that comparison to a real usability study isn't shown as having been done. The transferable move also says a synthetic panel walk should never stand in for the real device in the user's actual hands.",
